Mine Manager AI database schema management
===========================================

There are two deliberately separate database paths.

NEW EMPTY INSTALLATION
----------------------

The historical Alembic chain begins with a marker for a pre-existing database
and cannot build an empty database. From the backend directory, configure the
new empty PostgreSQL database in `.env`, then run:

    python -m app.scripts.bootstrap_v1_0_database \
        --confirm-empty-installation \
        --confirm-database-name <exact DB_NAME>

The command refuses Azure/blocked hosts and any database containing user
relations or Alembic state. It transactionally applies the immutable schema in
`schema/v1_0_c4e91a7b2d30.sql`, verifies the versioned structural contract,
stamps `c4e91a7b2d30`, and runs `alembic upgrade head`.

Never run the V1.0 bootstrap against an existing or partially initialized
database. It is not an upgrade or repair command.

EXISTING INSTALLATION
---------------------

For an existing database already managed by Alembic:

    alembic current
    alembic heads
    alembic upgrade head
    alembic current

Do not run the consolidated bootstrap and do not stamp a revision merely to
bypass a failed migration. Back up the database and follow the approved change
process before applying normal forward migrations.
